1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,691
Every Claude Code session starts from zero.

2
00:00:02,991 --> 00:00:06,754
NockBrain gives it a memory, and
nothing goes in until you approve it.

3
00:00:07,454 --> 00:00:08,743
Make a decision once.

4
00:00:09,043 --> 00:00:11,123
Days later, ask what you decided,

5
00:00:11,163 --> 00:00:13,753
and Claude answers from
your own reviewed notes.

6
00:00:14,453 --> 00:00:18,206
You choose the notes, or turn on a hook
that queues what was said in a session.

7
00:00:18,506 --> 00:00:19,783
Secrets are redacted.

8
00:00:20,083 --> 00:00:23,238
You read every candidate, then
apply it or throw it away.

9
00:00:23,538 --> 00:00:27,088
Applied facts are signed, and what
you approved is never rewritten.

10
00:00:27,788 --> 00:00:31,868
When a prompt asks about the past,
NockBrain checks every signature,

11
00:00:31,908 --> 00:00:34,268
ranks your current facts by shared words,

12
00:00:34,308 --> 00:00:38,005
and returns up to 800
tokens, labeled as reference.

13
00:00:38,705 --> 00:00:39,973
It runs on your machine.

14
00:00:40,273 --> 00:00:43,277
No network calls, no
model calls, no telemetry.

15
00:00:43,977 --> 00:00:46,617
The limit today: recall needs shared words,

16
00:00:46,657 --> 00:00:49,059
so a fact you phrase
differently won't come back.

17
00:00:49,759 --> 00:00:52,341
NockBrain is free and MIT licensed.

18
00:00:52,641 --> 00:00:54,670
Clone it and try it on your next session.
